{
  "info": {
    "name": "Waves - Ecommerce Backend API",
    "description": "Full API collection for the Waves e-commerce backend (Laravel 13). All request URLs are literal (no Postman variables). Base URL used throughout: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api\n\nTwo separate auth tokens are used: an Admin token (full access) and a Customer token (can only place/view their own orders). Replace the placeholder Bearer token text in each protected request with a real token obtained from the matching login request.\n\nProduct lifecycle extras: GET /admin/products/trashed (list soft-deleted), PATCH /admin/products/{id}/reassign (move to another category/brand - works even on trashed products), POST /admin/products/{id}/restore, DELETE /admin/products/{id}/force (permanent delete). Deleting a Category or Brand that still has products (even soft-deleted ones) returns 409 with a 'blocking_products' list instead of deleting.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Admin - Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Admin Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/admin/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin@12345\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Admin Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/admin/logout",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE",
                  "type": "string"
